IDENTIFICATION OF MAJOR PROTEINS ASSOCIATED WITH DICTYOSTELIUM
DISCOIDEUM ENDOCYTIC VESICLES

Celine Adessi, Agnes Chapel, Mathilde Vincon, Thierry Rabilloud,
Gerard Klein, Michel Satre and Jerome Garin

Departement de Biologie Moleculaire et Structurale, CEN-G, 17 rue des
Martyrs, 38054 Grenoble Cedex 09, France.

J. Cell Sci., in press

SUMMARY

   Magnetic isolation of endocytic vesicles from Dictyostelium
discoideum was accomplished after feeding the amoebae with iron oxide
particles. Proteins associated with the endocytic vesicles were
resolved by SDS-PAGE and digested "in-gel" with endoproteinase Lys-C
or Asp-N to generate peptides for amino acid sequencing. This strategy
allowed the identification of the major protein constituents of the
vesicles, namely the A, B, D, E and 110 kDa subunits of a vacuolar
type H+-ATPase, actin, a Rab 7-like GTPase, a p34 protein
corresponding to a new cysteine proteinase and the 25 kDa product of a
recently sequenced D.  discoideum open reading frame (Winckler, T.,
1995; GeneBank U20997).

